+# Implementation Plan: Equipment Availability
+
+**Spec**: [spec.md](spec.md)
+
+## Summary
+Add `availability(query)` to `RentalService` in `src/rental.ts`, reusing `parsePeriod` and `overlaps`. Export the new `AvailabilityQuery` type from `src/index.ts`. Tests in `test/rental.test.ts`; one README line.
+
+## Constitution Check (before and after design)
+- I No runtime deps: pass.
+- II Strict TS/ESM: pass; no `any`, tsconfig unchanged.
+- III Tests: pass; deterministic, `node:test`.
+- IV Explicit rules: pass; reuses the named overlap and period rules, no new domain rule guessed.
+- V Simplicity: pass; one method, no new abstraction.
+
+## Design
+- `AvailabilityQuery { start: string; end: string; kind?: EquipmentKind }`.
+- Validate period via `parsePeriod({ itemId: '', start, end })`-compatible helper (parsePeriod only reads start/end; widen its parameter to `{ start: string; end: string }`).
+- If `kind !== undefined` and not `'board'`/`'sail'`, throw `TypeError`.
+- Filter equipment by kind, drop items with an overlapping booking, map to ids, `.sort()`.
